# Sources of the photos on the details cards; tools/object_images/gen_images.py reads this file.
#
#   key|image URL|source page|credit|licence|crop
#     key      a deep-sky object's first id in deep_sky.txt (M31, NGC 253), @BODY for the Sun,
#              Moon or a planet (com.skyglass.astro.SkyBody name), or @PLANET/Name for one of
#              its moons; moons are listed innermost first, which is the gallery order
#     credit   as the source page gives it
#     licence  Public domain (NASA) or CC BY 4.0 (ESA/Hubble, ESA/Webb, ESO, NOIRLab)
#     crop     optional x0,y0,x1,y1 as fractions of the image, to frame the object
#   skip|key|reason   a deep-sky object deliberately left without a photo
#
# Chosen by hand, preferring a natural-colour view of the whole object (as in a telescope)
# over a close-up of part of it. Edit this file, then rerun gen_images.py.

# Sun, Moon and planets, then the planets' moons (NASA, public domain)

